I have a probably unworkable idea to make nethack for PC
rather faster to play.  One of the biggest waits is when
starting/saving/quiting. Couldnt the code be changed to
only extract the level info from the large save game 
file which you are in/entering, and only change those 
levels which have been entered or had monsters drop into
them when saving.  Im not a (good) programmer so I dont
know how easy this would be.
 
Monsters using items, I find it really annoying when the
monster uses one shot items (scrolls/potions) as soon as
they see you. I would like there to be at least some 
chance of getting the potion of gain level from the 
monster especially as if it only takes 1/2 attacks to
kill it.
 
This goes for some other items as well, How do monsters
'know' that a amulet of lifesaving is a good thing to 
wear, couldnt we have some chance of monsters not 
wearing stuff when they probably have no idea what it
does.
 
Oh a final thing on the savegame/startgame times. When
you get into the final levels, surely it is impossible
to return to the main dungeon and all the rest of the 
save game data can be scrapped. Cutting down on disk
space used and the time taken to load.
 
Erm finally it seems unfair that the random +2 to -2
level change for new man/new woman polymorphing can only
result in -ve change when you are already level 30.
Ditto for stat changes when you were 18/** 18 for the
lot.







